## Dependencies installed separately

This checkout does not contain Python or Node.js interpreters, a portable EXE,
a complete `site-packages` tree, `node_modules`, or private login SDK templates.
The dependency declarations are in `app/requirements.txt`,
`requirements-desktop.txt`, and both terrain-engine `package-lock.json` files.
Do not treat historical runtime-version lists as a reproducible environment.

The terrain locks declare these external dependency families:

- `@dimforge/rapier3d-compat` 0.21.0 — Apache-2.0;
  https://github.com/dimforge/rapier.js
- `recast-navigation`, `@recast-navigation/core`, `@recast-navigation/generators`
  and `@recast-navigation/wasm` 0.44.0 — MIT;
  https://github.com/isaac-mason/recast-navigation-js
- `meshoptimizer` 1.3.0 — MIT;
  https://github.com/zeux/meshoptimizer

Those packages are not vendored as installed dependencies in this checkout.
When assembling a binary distribution, retain the complete licenses and
notices from the actual packages being redistributed. A package's dependency
license is not changed by the root license metadata for the project's own
`xiaoguang-terrain-core` package.

Python requirements include NumPy, requests, cryptography, zstandard, PySocks,
psutil, Unicorn and Capstone. The desktop build adds pywebview and PyInstaller,
which may bring transitive dependencies. Their installed distribution metadata
and full original licenses must accompany any redistribution that requires
those notices; this source list is not a replacement for those texts.

The following original notice files are retained as reference material from
previous distribution work, not as a claim that their binaries are included:

- `THIRD_PARTY/capstone-5.0.9/LICENSE.TXT`;
- `THIRD_PARTY/unicorn-2.1.4/LICENSE` and `SOURCE-OFFER.txt`;
- the package license files under `THIRD_PARTY/Desktop/` for bottle, cffi,
  clr_loader, pythonnet and pywebview.

The historical Unicorn source-offer text refers to the earlier portable
package described in that text. This checkout includes no Unicorn binary.
The original offer is preserved without modifying any prior commitment;
see `THIRD_PARTY/unicorn-2.1.4/README.md` for that scope distinction.

## Source and resource boundaries

Research snapshots and validation artifacts mentioned in the terrain notices
are retained separately and are not shipped as a `research` directory here.
No game APK, extracted map geometry, compression dictionary, user account
cache, or private server configuration is supplied by this source checkout.
The root `NOTICE` retains the original distinction between project-owned work,
third-party materials and game resources. Missing provenance is not converted
into a blanket project copyright or license grant.

## 3dicons V1 desktop illustrations

The desktop embeds three unmodified 3dicons V1 clay PNGs (Star, Chat Bubble
and Map Pin), created by Vijay Verma / realvjy and dedicated under CC0 1.0.
They are local data URLs in `app/web/desktop.js`, not game assets. The complete
license and per-asset source URLs, hashes and dimensions are retained in
`THIRD_PARTY/3dicons-v1/LICENSE` and `THIRD_PARTY/3dicons-v1/sources.json`.
See that directory's README for the exact embedding location and provenance.
